meta {
  name: GetDashForm
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/npp/artikelscan?scan={{nppScanNummer}}-500
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq resolved
  res.body.article.artnr: isString
  res.body.article.aantal: eq 0.5
  res.body.empty: eq false
}

docs {
  GET /web/npp/artikelscan?scan=<nummer>-<milliAantal> - the
  "nummer-aantal" dash form (step 2 of
  Luna.BusinessLogic.NPPArtikelScanBE:ResolveScan, 1:1 port of
  \LHDC01\TESTLUNA$\LunaV12\CheckBarcode.p): splits on the first dash,
  parses the left side as INTEGER and looks it up against artikel.nummer
  (artikel-x09), parses the right side as DECIMAL and divides by 1000 for
  "aantal". Here "-500" -> aantal 0.5. Only this resolution path adds the
  "aantal" key to the "article" object - it's omitted entirely for every
  other resolution path.

  {{nppScanNummer}} must be set (collection/environment variable, not
  currently in Local.bru) to a real artikel.nummer value (INTEGER, not
  the artnr) from LunaNew.

  Read-only - backed by Backend/src/Luna/Web/NPPArtikelScanHandler.cls +
  Luna/BusinessLogic/NPPArtikelScanBE.cls.
}
